  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"rerun-sdk\" %}\n{% set version = \"0.36.0\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun/archive/refs/tags/{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: ccdabd90c7f6725c6ffd8b9a1fc1537815d514a48b2ce97eb15d2d783091de6f\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: true  # [py<38]\n  # nodejs doesn't support ppc64le\n  skip: true  # [ppc64le]\n  entry_points:\n    - rerun = rerun.__main__:main\n  # gilrs (gamepad support, new in rerun 0.34.0) links the always-present\n  # WinRT API-set umbrella DLL, which conda-build's overlinking check flags\n  missing_dso_whitelist:\n    - '*/api-ms-win-core-winrt-l1-1-0.dll'  # [win]\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - crossenv                               # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - maturin >=1.3.0                        # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ compiler('c') }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - {{ compiler('rust') }}  # [target_platform != \"osx-arm64\"]\n    - rust {{ rust_compiler_version }}  # [target_platform == \"osx-arm64\"]\n    - rust-std-aarch64-apple-darwin  # [target_platform == \"osx-arm64\"]\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - rust-std-wasm32-unknown-unknown\n    # binaryen gives us wasm-opt, for optimizing the an .wasm file for speed and size\n    - binaryen\n    - nodejs >=20.12\n    - nasm\n    # The web viewer cross-compiles native dependencies to wasm32. The build\n    # scripts scope these tools to that target so host compilers stay intact.\n    - clang\n    - llvm-tools\n    # needed to get protoc for to lance\n    - libprotobuf\n    # gilrs (gamepad support, new in rerun 0.34.0) uses libudev-sys on linux,\n    # which shells out to pkg-config at build time\n    - pkg-config  # [linux]\n  host:\n    - anywidget\n    - hatch\n    - hatch-jupyter-builder\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - maturin >=1.3.0\n    # provides libudev.pc / the udev library that gilrs-core links against.\n    # Cap below 258: libudev 258+ is built against glibc 2.34, but this\n    # feedstock builds against the c_stdlib 2.17 sysroot, so linking a\n    # 2.34 libudev.so fails the --no-allow-shlib-undefined check. 257.x\n    # is the newest series still built against glibc 2.17.\n    - libudev <258  # [linux]\n  run:\n    - python\n    - attrs >=23.1.0\n    - anywidget\n    - jupyter-ui-poll\n    - ipykernel <7.0.0\n    - numpy >=1.23\n    - pillow >=8.0.0\n    - psutil >=7.0\n    - pyarrow >=18.0.0\n    - typing_extensions >=4.5\n\n# TODO(jleibs): Would be nice to add this constraint, but it causes test to fail\n# to solve. Just live with the lack of constraint for now.\n#\n# run_constrained:\n#   - __glibc >=2.27                                        # [linux]\n\ntest:\n  requires:\n    - packaging\n\nabout:\n  home: https://www.rerun.io/\n  summary: Rerun is an SDK for logging computer vision and robotics data paired with a visualizer for exploring that data over time.\n  description: |\n    Rerun is an SDK for logging computer vision and robotics data paired with a visualizer for exploring that data over time.\n    It lets you debug and understand the internal state and data of your systems with minimal code.\n\n    Note: This conda package bundles both the functionality of the PyPI packages `rerun-sdk` and `rerun-notebook` as a single installable package.\n  license: MIT OR Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n    - LICENSE-MIT\n    - LICENSE-APACHE\n\n  doc_url: https://www.rerun.io/docs\n  dev_url: https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - oxkitsune\n    - aedm\n    - abey79\n    - ntjohnson1\n    - jeongseok-meta\n    - ruben-arts\n    - jleibs\n    - traversaro\n",
